# Line endings.
#
# The second development machine runs WSL2, where one checkout can be reached
# by both the Linux git inside the distro and the Windows git outside it. A
# Windows git with core.autocrlf=true rewrites files to CRLF on checkout, and
# bash then fails on every shell script in the repository with the error
# `\r: command not found` — scripts/verify.sh, scripts/eod-push.sh and each
# husky hook. Normalising here fixes it for every machine regardless of what
# that machine's core.autocrlf happens to be set to.
#
# Adding this cost nothing: on 2026-09-29 no tracked file had CRLF in the
# index, so there is no renormalisation diff hiding behind it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, and never to be touched by any of the above.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.jar   binary
*.keystore binary
